/**
 * @defgroup RoModular_Ecosystem Ecosystem
 * @brief Purpose, boundaries, and dependency architecture of RoModular.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup RoModular_Ecosystem_Overview Overview
 * @ingroup RoModular_Ecosystem
 * @brief What RoModular is and what belongs at the ecosystem level.
 *
 * RoModular organizes reusable software as small repositories with explicit
 * responsibilities. A repository should own one coherent domain and expose a
 * stable public contract to its consumers. Shared build mechanics belong in
 * RoModularBuild; project policy remains in the repository that owns the
 * resulting package.
 *
 * The ecosystem portal owns:
 *
 * - the catalog of repositories;
 * - the high-level dependency map;
 * - project maturity and compatibility status;
 * - links to source, API documentation, releases, and roadmaps; and
 * - cross-repository architectural decisions.
 *
 * It does not own library APIs, compiler flags, target support claims, package
 * contents, or release evidence. Those facts remain in the affected project.
 */

